          "as": "w2",
          "client": {
            "valid": true
          },
          "expect": {
            "result": "ok"
          }
        },
        {
          "il": {},
          "expect": [
            "w3",
            "w1"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "derivation": "W1, W2 and W3 are three withdrawals from exp-frames experiment 06's keyed privacy pool, the sender of all three, each on its own nullifier as its nonce key, so hegota-testnet's disjoint-keys admits them together (FP-12); their roots are at slots 323047, 323047 and 323020, all within the window at the head's current slot 323057. The pool's balance and the keys at 0 are the case's, as a replay reads no state. IL-2 at the next base fee, 7 by FEE-1 since the head used no gas: each has effective tip min(1, 100 - 7) = 1, so they are taken by arrival; each is a Profile 2 candidate with a budget of 410000. W3 leaves 638576 of 1048576, W1 228576, and W2's 410000 does not fit, so the list is [W3, W1]. Experiment 25's table B: two withdrawals for each list at their declared limits."
    },
